@node no1 " Introduction"

                    XIM Module for AmiExpress 2.xx - 3.xx

                      drewho is may the best lookin 
                    who door available at the moment...
                 it supports all features from Amixpress 
                       like QUIET Node and show the
                  Files who are transfered at the Moment

                            * Example Output: *

 Nd#       Name/Handle             Location/Group               Action         
.---.-------------------------------------------------------------------------.
| 0 | J.Walker               («*»»[*- T R S I -*]««*»)   UL: GVP-EGS1.DMS     |
| 1 | REDSKiN                >>>> tRSi & aRt <<<<        Scanning Mail...     |
| 2 | [-Dr.Dre!/tRSi]        ···====|·tRSi·|====···      Viewing other Nodes  |
`---^-----------------------------------------------------» drewho 1.o XiM «--'

in colour it looks much better...
@endnode
@node no2 " Requirements"

                You need an Amiga 500/1000/1200/2000/3000/4000
                          Kickstart 2.0 or higher
                     Ami Express 2.xx - 3.xx (Registered)

@endnode
@node no3 " Installation"

                  If you have /X 2.xx - 3.20 so copy the
                      drewho9.XiM File to your Doors
                      and the Who.Info to your BBSCmd
                 if you have /X 3.30++ running so take the
            drewho32.XiM Version this is the 32 Node Version !

                 NOTE: The Who.Info is configured for the
              32 Node Version if you use the 9 Node Version 
                    then you have to change the Icon...

have Phun...
@endnode
